# survey.param -- minimal delta set for the autonomous survey catamaran.
#
# ONLY parameters that differ from a stock ArduPilot Rover build belong here, so this file
# stays diffable and reviewable. The reasoning behind every row lives in verified.md; a
# value here without a row there is a value nobody can defend.
#
# Load with: Mission Planner / MAVProxy parameter load, then REBOOT (SCR_ENABLE needs it).
#
# Full dated dumps of the entire parameter set go in full/YYYY-MM-DD-context.param, taken
# BEFORE each session. This file is the delta; those are the record.
#
# INCOMPLETE. Only parameters whose values are actually established are listed. Everything
# still marked TODO in verified.md is deliberately absent rather than guessed -- see the
# TODO block at the bottom. Do not fill these in from memory; measure or read them off the
# board and update verified.md in the same commit.

# ---- Scripting ----
SCR_ENABLE,1
# Module selector: 0 = idle, 1 = mk1 dead-reckoning, 2 = mk2 GPS-anchored.
# Deployed as 0 so the boat never comes up already selecting a survey module.
SCR_USER1,0

# ---- Depth sensing ----
# Downward-facing rangefinder. Both modules test for orientation 25 before
# trusting a reading.
RNGFND1_ORIENT,25

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TODO: add once measured or read off the board, each with a verified.md row:
#
#   RNGFND1_TYPE       NMEA serial backend for the ATU120A (NOT the MAVLink
#                      type 10 used by the SITL feeders)
#   RNGFND1_MIN_CM     blocks F9 -- measure in the bucket test
#   RNGFND1_MAX_CM     must exceed the deepest water surveyed
#   SERIAL2_PROTOCOL   put TELEM2 on the rangefinder/NMEA protocol
#   SERIAL2_BAUD       must correspond to 4800 baud
#   WP_RADIUS          mk2 scales both arrival tests off it (F12)
#   WP_PIVOT_ANGLE     clean skid-steer pivots
#   WP_PIVOT_RATE      blocks F4 -- unverified on the board
#   FENCE_ENABLE       \
#   FENCE_RADIUS        |  must exceed MAX_LEG_DISTANCE_M = 60.0 m (F7)
#   FENCE_ACTION        |
#   FENCE_TYPE         /
#   BATT_MONITOR       \
#   BATT_FS_LOW_ACT     |  F11 -- blocks water test
#   BATT_LOW_VOLT       |
#   BATT_CRT_VOLT       |
#   BATT_FS_CRT_ACT    /
#
# Confirm the RNGFND1_MIN_CM / RNGFND1_MIN naming against the firmware actually
# on the board before adding those rows -- the names differ across versions and
# a wrong one reads back as nil in the scripts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
